# Build output
bin/
obj/
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
*.user
.vs/
.idea/

# Fetched Slang binaries. Never committed: ~36 MB per RID, and reproducible from the pin in
# Directory.Build.props via `pwsh tools/fetch-native.ps1`.
runtimes/

# Fetched PrismNRI packages. nupkg-feed/*.nupkg is ignored by that folder's own .gitignore rather
# than here, so the folder itself stays tracked and the local source nuget.config names always
# exists. Never committed for the same reason as runtimes/: reproducible from the PrismNriVersion
# pin in Directory.Build.props via `pwsh tools/fetch-nri.ps1`.

# dotnet/Native/ IS committed. It is generated by tools/generate-native.ps1, but committing it
# keeps the repo buildable without the ClangSharp tool installed, and — more importantly — makes
# a Slang version bump show up as a reviewable diff. Vtable reordering is a silent ABI break;
# reviewing that diff is the control. See docs/binding-surface.md §4.3.

# TRX from the filtered validation-layer run in CI (ci.yml). A build artefact, not a result.
vulkan-results/

# Test run output. CI produces these deliberately (results.trx feeds the crash-diagnostic step
# and the uploaded artifact); locally they are just noise from a run with a logger attached.
TestResults/
*.trx
